 <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,590.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,590.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,590.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,645.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,600.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Recover as Oil Marketers Watch Fuel Price Direction\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Oil prices rebounded on Wednesday after recent declines, prompting fresh attention across Nigeria's downstream petroleum market. As of 12:40 p.m. WAT on Wednesday , Brent crude traded at $80.40 per barrel , up 1.31%. U.S. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) rose 0.45% to $76.11 per barrel.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-recover-as-oil-marketers-watch-fuel-price-direction\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Indian Refiner Buys 2 Million Barrels of Nigerian Crude for September\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    India's Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Limited (HPCL) has selected two of Nigeria's premium crude blends, Utapate and Okwuibome, to supply its Rajasthan refinery in September. According to Reuters, citing trade sources, HPCL secured two million barrels of the Nigerian crude from commodities trader Glencore. The cargoes are scheduled for delivery in late September.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/indian-refiner-buys-2-million-barrels-of-nigerian-crude-for-september\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Vessel Arrivals: Matrix, NNPCL, AYM Shafa, Others Receive Fresh PMS, AGO, LPG Cargoes\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Fresh cargoes of Premium Motor Spirit (PMS), Automotive Gas Oil (AGO), Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) and Jet A1 continue to arrive at Nigeria's coastal petroleum terminals. The sustained inflow reflects marketers' continued efforts to maintain product availability despite fluctuating international oil prices.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/vessel-arrivals-matrix-nnpcl-aym-shafa-others-receive-fresh-pms-ago-lpg-cargoes\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery Targets $5bn October IPO to Accelerate Africa’s Fuel Independence\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Africa's largest oil refinery, the Dangote Petroleum Refinery, is preparing to raise about $5 billion through an initial public offering (IPO) expected in October. The landmark listing is set to become one of the largest capital market transactions in Africa and will provide fresh funding to expand operations.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-targets-5bn-october-ipo-to-accelerate-africas-fuel-independence\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Crash 5% as Markets Bet on US-Iran Deal Despite Hormuz Threats\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $79.39 per barrel, down 5.23%, while US West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude stood at $75.86 per barrel. The renewed weakness in crude prices followed comments from US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and Qatar's Foreign Ministry suggesting that progress was being made on a draft framework.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-crash-5-as-markets-bet-on-us-iran-deal-despite-hormuz-threats\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
